#
# `:existsSubselectLimit` fixture: two subjects, each with its OWN single `:q`
# fact. `FILTER EXISTS { SELECT ?s WHERE { ?s :q ?y } LIMIT 1 }` correlates via
# the sub-`SELECT`'s own projected `?s` (`Project`-boundary narrowing keeps the
# substitution), with `LIMIT 1` sitting ABOVE the substitution site — a shape the
# probe strategy cannot answer correctly by evaluating the whole `LIMIT 1`
# UNCONSTRAINED once (that single evaluation can only keep ONE of `:s1`/`:s2`'s
# rows, dropping the other), while the definition path re-evaluates the
# substituted, single-value-restricted pattern PER outer row, so `LIMIT 1` always
# has its own value's match to keep — both `:s1` and `:s2` must survive.
@prefix : <https://example.org/exists#> .

:s1 :p :o1 .
:s2 :p :o2 .
:s1 :q :vA .
:s2 :q :vB .
